 a major  milestone that we think is important to  customers these are things like dremel X  which we'll talk about in a moment and  some of the other things that we've done  around faster data ingestion and better  support for the sequel language that's  five years of innovation but what have  we done lately well to take a look at  this we first have to take a look at big  queries architecture now importantly  bigquery dis aggregates storage and  compute now this allows us some real  advantages we can summon thousands of  virtual CPUs in an instant to service a  query however this is all dependent on  Google's incredibly fast data center  networking because our networks have a  pet a bit by section it means that even  though that storage is separate from  compute it runs as if it was all in the  same gigantic machine so that pata bite  can be scanned and processed incredibly  quickly now one of the improvements we  made was to the way that Dremel actually  allocates these virtual CPUs to the task  at hand let's take a look at the Dremel  architecture from 2006 to 2015 now in  this case we relied on what we called a  long live serving tree now this looks  very similar to those of you coming from  the database world to a directed acyclic  processing graph or a query plan and  that's exactly what it is now this was  very useful in terms of being able to  simply scan and process lots of data for  common queries however for certain kinds  of queries maybe wasn't ideal so  recently we produce something called  Dremel X and this architecture is much  more dynamic you can think about this as  Dremel optimizer or big queries  optimizer getting much smarter about how  to allocate compute units in an instant  to the queries at hand now what does  this mean for you this means massive  joins get faster most queries got an  order of magnitude faster and everything  just works and revel ax is available as  part of bigquery now users who switch to  the systems didn't even know they  switched they just woke up and queries  got much faster and we continue to make  improvements like this to bigquery every  day now we've talked a little bit about  how bigquery takes advantage of a legacy  of big data advances inside Google but  where does it fit within Google cloud  platforms data architecture or your own  data architecture let's take a look now  if we zoom in one of the things we might  really care about is the fundamentals of  data warehousing or big data systems  where do i load and store data and then  how am I going to analyze and understand  that data now if we look at the load and  store side of the house you can see  three things that really form the heart  of that part of our reference  architecture you have google cloud  dataflow which is used for etl streaming  aggregation and a number of other things  you have google cloud storage which is  designed for incredibly low cost planet  scale storage and then we have systems  like Google big table which is designed  for IOT data time series and other  things that tend to be calm family in  nature now on the analysis side we've  got big query which obviously we've been  talking quite a lot about but for those  of you who want to take advantage of the  open source big data space like a dupe  and spark we offer Google Cloud Data  proc and this allows you to run the  latest versions of Hadoop and spark in a  fully managed cluster in seconds I have  an arrow between these two things it  says full integration what does that  mean well full integration does means  that I don't have to draw little arrows  between each of these hexagons to tell  you this thing connects to that this  other thing connects this way you can  only do this with this other thing  full integration means all of these  products in Google cloud platform are  designed to work together seamlessly  without any extra effort on your part  but what about other things there are  other things that we do with data other  than load and store it and analyze and  understand it so let's take a bit of a  broader look we want you to be able to  ingest data into Google cloud platform  from anywhere and we do this in part  through technologies like our own google  cloud pub/sub which allows you to do  scalable message queue in from anywhere  in the world but also to tools that you  may use today like ETL tools such as  talent or data wrangling tools like  trifecta and on the other side we know  that it's important that you be able to  visualize data the way that you want to  explore it easily and share it with  others which is why both bigquery and  Google Cloud Data proc are fully  integrated with solutions like tableau  and MicroStrategy as well as with our  own solutions such as Google Analytics  360 and it's data studio 360 project and  with things like Google Cloud Data lab  which provides data scientists a  flexible environment to both write their  own code and integrate with systems like  bigquery now we talked earlier in this  webcast about the fact that bigquery is  fully managed what is fully managed mean  we think fully managed means getting  more it means that as a big query user  you get solutions like dynamic execution  immediately you wake up one day and  bigquery just got a lot faster your  queries got easier to write it also  means things like project Poseidon come  to you and you wake up and things get  better the Sidon allows you to all of a  sudden load new kinds of files such as a  bro file formats it also means that most  ingestions got 10 times faster you get  this all just one day without having to  do anything and then things like  consistent scheduling as we mentioned  big queries architecture allows us to  some of the vast number of CPUs  instantaneously to service your query  but at the same time we make sure you're  always going to have more than enough  resources to handle your queries it's a  fully managed means you get the latest  innovations without having to go through  painful upgrades whether it's on the  query execution side or the data storage  side it also means you always have the  resources you need to process your data  now I'm going to throw it back to chat  is going to talk a little bit more about  other partners and how they integrate  with Google  query  bigquery isn't trying to be everything  to everyone in places where we're not  building functionality we need to  partner with outstanding companies to  provide that functionality to our  customers you can see here four  different functional areas from  visualization to data preparation it's  important for bigquery to use these  other technologies so that you as a  company if you use MicroStrategy or if  you use talent or tableau you can still  use those tools but have bigquery as  your back-end thanks for taking the time  to watch the webinar on behalf of my  other speakers I just wanted to extend  that thank you and if you're curious  about learning more you can go to cloud  google.com / bigquery take care  [Music]
 

